diff --git a/guest/README.md b/guest/README.md
index 02edab5..f0e16f4 100644
--- a/guest/README.md
+++ b/guest/README.md
@@ -46,3 +46,36 @@ The output includes the kernel, initramfs, raw and compressed ext4 image,
 provenance, package inventory, licenses, manifest, and SHA-256 sums. Generated
 output belongs under the repository's ignored `dist/` directory and must not be
 committed.
+
+## QEMU cursor package
+
+Aquamarine is a managed same-name rebuild, `0.15.1-1.1`, of Arch's locked
+`0.15.1-1`. The upstream source archive, hotspot patch and builder digest are
+in `supplyChain.aquamarine`. The build uses the locked guest compiler, headers,
+CMake and hyprwayland-scanner, retains Arch's versioned dependencies and
+`libaquamarine.so=14-64` provide, and checks that Hyprland loads afterward.
+Provenance records source/build pins and package/library digests.
+
+The local repository stays after Arch. Runtime `4.0.4-10` has a minimum
+`aquamarine>=0.15.1-1.1` dependency, so the first Update > Omarchy on an old disk
+selects the local rebuild if Arch has not moved. Further normal updates keep
+it while Arch is unchanged. A newer Arch package release or source version
+wins normally, including a coordinated Hyprland/SONAME update; there is no
+IgnorePkg, exact-version hold, custom provider or pre-transaction replacement.
+The patch can disappear after that bump, restoring the previous in-frame cursor
+behavior while allowing the desktop upgrade. The real libalpm fixture tests
+cover these transactions and run a linked consumer after each upgrade.
+
+To re-pin after an Arch bump, refresh the package lock, adapt and review the
+hotspot patch against the new source, update its source/patch/builder digests,
+SONAME/provide and `archVersion`, and set `packageVersion` to the new Arch
+version plus `.1`. Raise the runtime package release and compatibility revision
+so existing disks receive the newer authenticated offer. Run the guest contract,
+real transaction tests and complete image build/boot before shipping.
+
+Compatibility revision 61 delivers `cursor:use_cpu_buffer=1` inside the QEMU
+profile only, preserving customized or linked monitor configs through existing
+catch-up rules. This keeps virgl sprites upright and leaves `invisible=false`.
+The matching QEMU host cursor work is separate; this guest change is groundwork,
+not Windows SDL acceptance. Share this patch and profile with the Linux port;
+its SDL presentation still needs its own validation.
